From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0398-sweep-02-hang-watch.patch

Source: 0398-sweep-02-hang-watch.patch
Moved by hand: the pipeline note moved after upstream's new bind_pipeline line; scheduler includes merged

vulkan: EDEN_NX2_HANG_WATCH=1 names the unfinished submissions of a stalled GPU wait

Port of the HANG_WATCH part of pavelgajdo/Lichii-Android 492774519b (pavelgajdo, 2026-11-05).
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core. Its EDEN_NX2_SPIRV_DUMP part is not ported.

A wait for a GPU tick that lasts 3 s logs the waited tick, the tick the GPU reached, the last one
submitted and the pipelines of every unfinished submission. Submitted and never finished is a
GPU-side hang; never submitted is an emulator deadlock. Stages print as in the source, s0 to s5 by
unique_hashes index and s6 for compute, so logs compare with the Android ones.

Changed from the source:
- One 3 s timed wait, then the plain wait, not 3 s waits in a loop. On the PS5 each timed wait
  restarts RADV's 10 s no-progress check (radv_ps5_queue_wait_seq, mihawk-99/PS5_Mesa f5610fe), so
  the source's loop would turn a hung GPU from device lost into a wait with no end. With the switch
  on device lost comes after about 13 s instead of 10 s. One report per wait, not one per 3 s.
- This core has no TraceGraphicsPipeline or TraceComputePipeline. The notes sit in ConfigureDraw,
  when bind_pipeline is set, and in ComputePipeline::Configure. A mesh draw run as compute passes
  goes through ConfigureDraw too, so its hashes are in the same submission.
- Hashes are kept raw and formatted only in a report, not one string per bind. 256 pipelines per
  submission, not 64, with the number not kept in the report.
- ReportStall takes its lock with try_to_lock, copies and logs without it. Full lists for the first
  4 reports, nothing after 64.
- The switch is read once in the Scheduler constructor. EDEN_NX2_HANG_WATCH=0 is off.
- The members sit before worker_thread, which uses them until it stops.
- The SubmitExecution hook sits after on_submit: prepare-vulkan-port.py anchors on cmdbuf.End()
  directly followed by on_submit, and a missed anchor is only skipped, which would lose GpuTimeEnd.

Off: nothing recorded, no lock, no allocation, on_stall empty. The cost is a test of a bool per
pipeline bind, dispatch and submission. MasterSemaphore::Wait tests on_stall only after its fast
checks, where it is about to block anyway.

It adds no wait: the timed wait replaces the start of the plain one. Not run; timed waits on the PS5
read in radv_ps5_sync.c only. Memory with the switch on: at most about 1 MB. Off: under 200 bytes
in Scheduler.

Co-authored-by: pavelgajdo <234912265+pavelgajdo@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

